plugins/atlas-sidecar-excel/desk_bridge.py follows the loopback-bridge security design of Workbench
(hermes-office-desktop, Apache-2.0, same author): 127.0.0.1-only bind, exact add-in origin, Host check,
bounded bodies, metadata-only logs.

The sidebar loads Microsoft's Office.js from appsforoffice.microsoft.com at run time; it is not included here.
Bundled npm dependencies keep their own licenses (see package-lock.json): marked (MIT),
DOMPurify (Apache-2.0 or MPL-2.0), and PapaParse (MIT). Retain webpack-generated
taskpane.*.js.LICENSE.txt in the published site.

